For any subsystem of D, the filter induced by that subsystem confirms the neighbourhood generated by js exactly when the subsystem confirms every basic neighbourhood named by an index of js.

If the induced filter confirms the neighbourhood, the witnessing list determines the same finitely generated family, so the generator-wise criterion transfers membership from that list to js. Conversely, the list js itself, together with the assumed generator memberships, is a witness that the induced filter confirms the neighbourhood.
